WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.859
Move to the work list and open a task from the approved plan.

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:08.632
Its crop, location, planned quantity, and checklist provide the reporting context.

00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:10.690
We will demonstrate a short result.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:16.178
The quantity entered next is an example report, not a measurement collected from a real farm.

00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:27.874
Enter a quantity one unit below the task's plan, complete the checklist, and type a clear note explaining the shortage.

00:00:27.874 --> 00:00:29.734
Then save the reported result.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:33.082
Notice that this is labelled farmer reported and unverified.

00:00:33.082 --> 00:00:37.546
The short result prompts recovery instead of silently rewriting the original projection.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:49.451
If a scale reading was wrong, record a correction with a reason.

00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:53.768
Here we revise the reported quantity and explain that the scale was checked.

00:00:53.768 --> 00:00:57.088
Save auditable correction preserves the history of the first report.

00:00:57.088 --> 00:01:00.409
The updated value remains a report, with its provenance intact.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.951
The next decision is Compare recovery plans.

00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:12.502
Open it to inspect a future change while keeping completed work in history.

00:01:12.502 --> 00:01:16.353
We review the proposal and close it without applying another change.

00:01:16.353 --> 00:01:21.255
Recovery is deliberate: opening a form or reading advice does not approve additional work.
